<title>USA: Peak IPO postponed -- underwriter.</title>
<headline>Peak IPO postponed -- underwriter.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The planned initial public offering in Peak International Ltd was postponed due to market conditions, lead underwriter Donaldson Lufkin &amp; Jenrette said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The initial public offering, expected to trade within the week of April 14, proposed to offer three million shares at an estimated price range of $12 to $14 per share under the proposed symbol of &quot;PITLF&quot; on the Nasdaq National Market.</p>
<p>Peak, based in Hong Kong, supplies precision engineered packaging products for the storage, transportation and automated handling of semiconductor devices and other electronic components.</p>
</text>
